Corrected message:

Fix Cut/Erase baking objects without a clipped modifier's effect

When a selection-driven raster operation (Cut, Erase, moving selected
pixels, and similar) baked only the objects under the selection, it
checked whether the selection reached a clipped modifier, not whether
the modifier's clip reached those objects. A clip that missed the
selection but overlapped a baked object let that object's raw pixels,
without the modifier applied, be committed into the layer. That case
now bakes the whole stack instead, with the usual confirmation. The
overlap check uses bounds only, so it may ask more often than needed
but never misses.

Also free the full-canvas scratch surface that the object-subset bake
leaked on every call.
